00:24:23.180 --> 00:24:26.180
And the treasure, which is supposedly millions in gold bars.

00:24:26.180 --> 00:24:27.180
And given the rate of inflation,

00:24:27.180 --> 00:24:29.339
We're talking the motherload of all buried booty.

00:24:29.339 --> 00:24:31.180
More than enough to kill your best friend over.

00:24:31.180 --> 00:24:32.180
And anyone else.

00:24:32.180 --> 00:24:56.009
Don't tell me you're leaving.

00:24:56.009 --> 00:24:59.009
I thought I needed more help than just my makeup.

00:24:59.009 --> 00:25:03.150
Maybe my cousin is right.

00:25:03.150 --> 00:25:06.430
I'm going here.

00:25:06.430 --> 00:25:08.430
I'm sorry I was harsh on you.

00:25:08.430 --> 00:25:11.430
But that was before I knew you were special.

00:25:11.430 --> 00:25:13.430
I saw you care.

00:25:13.430 --> 00:25:15.430
You're a very talented girl.

00:25:15.430 --> 00:25:18.430
Now, I'm just like everyone else.

00:25:18.430 --> 00:25:21.430
No, you're not you.

00:25:21.430 --> 00:25:22.430
You.

00:25:22.430 --> 00:25:25.430
have powers just like us.

00:25:25.430 --> 00:25:28.809
You have...

00:25:28.809 --> 00:25:29.809
How?

00:25:29.809 --> 00:25:34.569
Let's just say we were in the right place at the right time

00:25:34.569 --> 00:25:36.569
during the last meteor show.

00:25:36.569 --> 00:25:40.849
But the important thing is, is you're not alone, Kara.

00:25:40.849 --> 00:25:42.849
And we need you.

00:25:42.849 --> 00:25:46.849
We're going on a treasure hunt

00:25:46.849 --> 00:25:50.849
to find the time capsule, but we can't do it without you.

00:25:50.849 --> 00:25:53.849
Here's a photo of the gold before it was stolen.

00:25:53.849 --> 00:25:55.849
It's more than enough to buy a new prona bag

00:25:55.849 --> 00:25:58.849
I'm proud of bag every season for the rest of our lives.

00:25:58.849 --> 00:26:16.630
All we want to do is get that mat.

00:26:16.630 --> 00:26:17.630
Help me in.

00:26:17.630 --> 00:26:19.910
Baby.

00:26:19.910 --> 00:26:37.019
Little Miss Sunshine double-crossed us.

00:26:37.019 --> 00:26:54.630
...Walker, Cara Kett, Kelly Carson,

00:26:54.630 --> 00:27:07.740
Elizabeth Johnson, Barry, Amy Harris,

00:27:07.740 --> 00:27:15.079
Sir Grinshaw.

00:27:15.079 --> 00:27:20.500
Great.

00:27:20.500 --> 00:27:28.960
Thank you, ladies.

00:27:28.960 --> 00:27:29.960
That was lovely, huh?

00:27:29.960 --> 00:27:31.960
And in just a moment, we'll announce

00:27:31.960 --> 00:27:33.960
Smallville's newest Miss Sweetcorn!

00:27:33.960 --> 00:27:42.019
I've been looking for her because I believe she saved me,

00:27:42.019 --> 00:27:44.019
not just from the river.

00:27:44.019 --> 00:27:47.019
I'm talking about much more than that, Carter.

00:27:47.019 --> 00:27:51.400
She saved me from drowning in the evil of my ways.

00:27:51.400 --> 00:27:58.490
What, Angel?

00:27:58.490 --> 00:28:00.490
No mortal woman pulled me from that river.

00:28:00.490 --> 00:28:10.819
She doesn't exist, so you can stop looking for her.

00:28:10.819 --> 00:28:15.329
Perhaps I can help you refocus on your real target.

00:28:15.329 --> 00:28:17.329
The spaceship you found.

00:28:17.329 --> 00:28:19.329
Wasn't the first to land in Smallville.

00:28:19.329 --> 00:28:26.329
My work at the dam, three years of research,

00:28:26.329 --> 00:28:31.329
300 gigabytes, all an attempt to prevent what I believe is coming.

00:28:31.329 --> 00:28:34.329
What I fear is inevitable.

00:28:34.329 --> 00:28:37.329
If you research is so inflammatory, why incriminate yourself?

00:28:37.329 --> 00:28:40.329
Well, given the magnitude of the project,

00:28:40.329 --> 00:28:44.329
I think it's time to reach out to the government for help.

00:28:44.329 --> 00:28:47.329
I mean, we are on the same side, aren't we?

00:28:47.329 --> 00:29:01.900
Now, ladies and gentlemen, the most people.

00:29:01.900 --> 00:29:04.900
The moment, you've all been waiting for,

00:29:04.900 --> 00:29:10.460
Smallville's new, Miss, Sweet Corn, Caracent!

00:29:10.460 --> 00:29:27.579
Thank you so much.

00:29:27.579 --> 00:29:30.579
You've made a newcomer feel so welcome.

00:29:30.579 --> 00:29:34.579
Hold on. Please, everybody, stay seated.

00:29:34.579 --> 00:29:38.579
I'm going to have to ask you to come with me, Miss.

00:29:38.579 --> 00:29:40.579
What's happening?

00:29:40.579 --> 00:29:42.579
Your friends tipped us off.

00:29:42.579 --> 00:29:48.049
Caracant, you're under arrest.

00:29:48.049 --> 00:30:00.289
Didn't you learn anything?

00:30:00.289 --> 00:30:03.289
Breaking into the time capsule, what were you thinking?

00:30:03.289 --> 00:30:06.289
I was thinking I had to get to that map before anyone else did.

00:30:06.289 --> 00:30:08.289
You shouldn't have stolen the map at all.

00:30:08.289 --> 00:30:15.349
Even if the treasure it leads to is Kryptonian?

00:30:15.349 --> 00:30:16.349
Why wouldn't you tell me?

00:30:16.349 --> 00:30:19.599
Where do you want me to start?

00:30:19.599 --> 00:30:23.599
You're patronizing watermelon tutorials, your reprimand,

00:30:23.599 --> 00:30:27.599
or your general disinterest in everything I've done since I showed up.

00:30:27.599 --> 00:30:28.599
Where is it?

00:30:28.599 --> 00:30:29.599
I'll show you.

00:30:29.599 --> 00:30:31.599
No, no, no.

00:30:31.599 --> 00:30:32.599
Let me stay here.

00:30:32.599 --> 00:30:34.599
Until Chloe can get you out legally.

00:30:34.599 --> 00:30:35.599
Just give me the map.

00:30:35.599 --> 00:30:36.599
I can't.

00:30:36.599 --> 00:30:37.599
Why not?

00:30:37.599 --> 00:30:41.599
When the sheriff dragged me away, there was some free gust of winds and blew it away.

00:30:41.599 --> 00:30:42.599
Okay, it's all right. It's all right.

00:30:42.599 --> 00:30:44.599
Sounds like one of the weather girls.

00:30:44.599 --> 00:30:47.599
Look, just tell us what you saw on the map.

00:30:47.599 --> 00:30:50.599
Keep digging. It should be there.

00:30:50.599 --> 00:30:56.480
There's no way there's gold in here.

00:30:56.480 --> 00:30:58.480
Maybe it's diamonds.

00:30:58.480 --> 00:31:04.329
Well, there better be something good in this box.

00:31:04.329 --> 00:31:12.539
It doesn't belong to you.

00:31:12.539 --> 00:31:34.289
It does now.

00:31:34.289 --> 00:31:36.289
You're not as tough as you talk.

00:31:36.289 --> 00:31:57.490
But I am.

00:31:57.490 --> 00:31:58.490
Dare, be careful.

00:31:58.490 --> 00:32:00.490
These rocks can kill you.

00:32:00.490 --> 00:32:16.470
I'm so sorry I didn't listen to you.

00:32:16.470 --> 00:32:20.140
But once I'm not.

00:32:20.140 --> 00:32:22.140
You saved me.

00:32:22.140 --> 00:32:26.640
And even though it's not the way I would have done it,

00:32:26.640 --> 00:32:31.950
I know that you need to figure out how to use your abilities your own way.

00:32:31.950 --> 00:32:34.950
Does that mean you're going to stop trying to tell me what to do?

00:32:34.950 --> 00:32:38.549
Probably not.

00:32:38.549 --> 00:32:39.549
Isn't that what family's for?

00:32:39.549 --> 00:32:53.829
This can't be.

00:32:53.829 --> 00:32:54.829
be from your ship.

00:32:54.829 --> 00:32:57.829
He was buried over 100 years ago.

00:32:57.829 --> 00:32:58.829
And I don't recognize a symbol.

00:32:58.829 --> 00:33:04.190
I think it's a code.

00:33:04.190 --> 00:33:05.190
Some kind of SOS.

00:33:05.190 --> 00:33:07.190
From who?

00:33:07.190 --> 00:33:10.190
I don't know.

00:33:10.190 --> 00:33:14.190
But if this is still on Earth, so is the Kryptonian that left it.

00:33:14.190 --> 00:33:25.039
Exactly how many of us have been here on this planet.

00:33:25.039 --> 00:33:29.039
I'm starting to think that Earth might play a bigger role in our father's plans than we

00:33:29.039 --> 00:33:31.769
realize.

00:33:31.769 --> 00:33:33.769
For now, all we can do is try to figure out who left this.

00:33:33.769 --> 00:33:34.769
In the meantime.

00:33:34.769 --> 00:33:37.769
I'll be fitting in.

00:33:37.769 --> 00:33:42.269
And if this doesn't say Smallville,

00:33:42.269 --> 00:33:44.269
I don't know what does.

00:33:44.269 --> 00:33:48.269
It is a big demotion, though, from his sweet corn to coffee jockey.

00:33:48.269 --> 00:33:51.779
No, you'll adjust.

00:33:51.779 --> 00:33:53.779
Just don't expect me to keep looking over my shoulder

00:33:53.779 --> 00:33:56.779
living this life of suffocating repression just because you do.

00:33:56.779 --> 00:33:58.779
Suffocating repression, huh?

00:33:58.779 --> 00:34:01.779
Hey, it's your language. I just studied it.

00:34:01.779 --> 00:34:07.380
Our language. You're one of us now.

00:34:07.380 --> 00:34:08.380
Us?

00:34:08.380 --> 00:34:13.030
Callow. Clark.

00:34:13.030 --> 00:34:16.030
You're not human.

00:34:16.030 --> 00:34:18.030
No matter how much you want to be.

00:34:18.030 --> 00:34:21.030
We can harvest corn and we can pump mocha's all we want,

00:34:21.030 --> 00:34:24.030
but it's not going to make us one of them.

00:34:24.030 --> 00:34:28.030
I may have been born on another planet to care, but Earth is my home.

00:34:28.030 --> 00:34:32.030
Everyone I love. Everyone I care about is here.

00:34:32.030 --> 00:34:34.030
It's where I belong.

00:34:34.030 --> 00:34:36.030
What about in 50 years?

00:34:36.030 --> 00:34:41.380
Look, we both know what's going to happen to everyone that you love.

00:34:41.380 --> 00:34:46.380
I'm sorry, but if you think you can just spend your life hiding here on the farm

00:34:46.380 --> 00:34:51.489
and growing old with Lana, you're fooling yourself.

00:34:51.489 --> 00:35:27.659
What do you have for me?

00:35:27.659 --> 00:35:29.659
We found her.

00:35:29.659 --> 00:35:40.590
Just where you said she would be.

00:35:40.590 --> 00:35:41.590
Congratulations.

00:35:41.590 --> 00:35:43.590
You just delivered a front page freak story.

00:35:43.590 --> 00:35:46.590
I'm just glad you finally out of the frozen food section.

00:35:46.590 --> 00:35:54.539
You know, when we first got together, I thought that you were pretty prejudiced.

00:35:54.539 --> 00:35:58.539
Quick to jump to the conclusion that some meteor infection

00:35:58.539 --> 00:36:03.980
Meteor-infected murder was behind every bad thing that happened in Smallville.

00:36:03.980 --> 00:36:04.980
Jimmy...

00:36:04.980 --> 00:36:06.980
But you're right.

00:36:06.980 --> 00:36:11.980
I've seen enough now to know that sooner or later they all snap.

00:36:11.980 --> 00:36:18.570
So from now on, it's open season in the infected.

00:36:18.570 --> 00:36:20.570
What do you say we clean up this town, partner?

00:36:20.570 --> 00:36:28.110
Sorry, I just came back from my bag.

00:36:28.110 --> 00:36:40.500
Why don't we go upstairs?

00:36:40.500 --> 00:36:43.010
Okay.

00:36:43.010 --> 00:36:56.989
You have no idea how good it feels to be back here,

00:36:56.989 --> 00:36:58.989
despite everything that's happened lately.

00:36:58.989 --> 00:37:01.230
Everything meaning Kara?

00:37:01.230 --> 00:37:04.989
Meeting your cousin has definitely been an experience,

00:37:04.989 --> 00:37:07.989
but I was talking more about what's going on with us.

00:37:07.989 --> 00:37:11.989
Clark, I was afraid that you wouldn't forgive me for marrying legs.

00:37:11.989 --> 00:37:13.989
Or for leaving.

00:37:13.989 --> 00:37:18.369
Mauna, nothing could ever change the way I feel about you.

00:37:18.369 --> 00:37:22.380
I've made so many mistakes.

00:37:22.380 --> 00:37:24.380
We've both made mistakes.

00:37:24.380 --> 00:37:28.980
This is our chance to start over.

00:37:28.980 --> 00:37:34.309
I just hope you know what you're getting into.

00:37:34.309 --> 00:37:38.260
I know exactly what I'm getting into.

00:37:38.260 --> 00:37:39.260
getting into.

00:37:39.260 --> 00:37:43.800
Look, I came back here for you.

00:37:43.800 --> 00:37:47.559
For us.

00:37:47.559 --> 00:37:53.820
I never want to let the past come between us again.

00:37:53.820 --> 00:37:56.820
I want us to wake up every morning and be there for each other.

00:37:56.820 --> 00:38:03.780
I want to grow.

00:38:03.780 --> 00:38:22.300
Tell me it's not too late for a cappuccine.

00:38:22.300 --> 00:38:27.730
Um, sorry, we're closed.

00:38:27.730 --> 00:38:28.730
Even for the owner?

00:38:28.730 --> 00:38:35.019
Technically, I don't even work here yet.

00:38:35.019 --> 00:38:36.019
At least not until tomorrow.

00:38:36.019 --> 00:38:39.019
I just came down to pick up the bag that I left.

00:38:39.019 --> 00:38:41.019
I want to thank you for safe.

00:38:41.019 --> 00:38:44.019
I want to thank you for saving my life.

00:38:44.019 --> 00:38:46.019
I know it was you.

00:38:46.019 --> 00:38:48.019
At the river?

00:38:48.019 --> 00:38:51.019
I think you've had me confused of someone else.

00:38:51.019 --> 00:38:56.969
You ripped the roof off my car.

00:38:56.969 --> 00:38:58.969
You must have been through a terrible ordeal.

00:38:58.969 --> 00:39:06.860
You were there. It's okay.

00:39:06.860 --> 00:39:09.860
I won't tell anyone, I promise.

00:39:09.860 --> 00:39:12.860
Your secret saved with me.

00:39:12.860 --> 00:39:14.860
I've already protected you.

00:39:14.860 --> 00:39:19.179
Like I would have protected others close to me

00:39:19.179 --> 00:39:20.179
if they would have told me the truth.

00:39:20.179 --> 00:39:24.699
This time I'm hoping to change all that.

00:39:24.699 --> 00:39:26.699
I just need you to be honest with me.

00:39:26.699 --> 00:39:31.940
Look, I'm sorry, Mr. Luther.

00:39:31.940 --> 00:39:35.940
The only secret I've got is that I make a lousy cappuccino.

00:39:35.940 --> 00:39:38.940
It's probably not the best thing to confess to your boss.

00:39:38.940 --> 00:39:43.179
Twice I've been pulled back from the brink of death.

00:39:43.179 --> 00:39:47.179
Both times it was by a member of the Kent family.

00:39:47.179 --> 00:39:52.099
I'm not a man who believes in coincidences.

00:39:52.099 --> 00:40:01.019
Sooner or later, I'll find out the truth.

00:40:01.019 --> 00:40:07.500
Are you a savior?

00:40:07.500 --> 00:40:08.500
Or are you a warning?

